# Patch:     020-field-cfg-raw-data-serializable-supertrait
# Phase:     pre-extraction
# Target:    field/src/extension/binomial_extension.rs, field/src/extension/cubic_extension.rs, field/src/extension/quintic_extension.rs, field/src/field.rs, symmetric/src/serializing_hasher.rs
# Hunks:     11
# Cost:      none in a normal build (see below). In the extracted variant,
#            `Field` no longer implies `RawDataSerializable`.
# Upstream:  charon#1266 (RPITIT/GAT lift is out of scope for
#            `--lift-associated-types`); aeneas has no GAT model.
# Drop when: charon lifts RPITIT to a named associated type, or aeneas models
#            GATs.
#
# Every method of `RawDataSerializable` except `NUM_BYTES` returns
# `impl IntoIterator`. rustc desugars each one into a hidden generic
# associated type on the trait, and `--preset=aeneas` cannot lift GATs.
# Charon writes type errors into the LLBC, and aeneas then fails on every
# item that mentions `Field`, which is nearly all of p3-baby-bear (803
# errors). The trait is only reached through `Field`'s supertrait list.
#
# The edge now goes through `FieldRawData`:
#   normal build:          trait FieldRawData: RawDataSerializable {}   + blanket impl
#   cfg(hax_backend_lean): trait FieldRawData {}                        + blanket impl
# Supertraits are transitive, so in a normal build `F: Field` still implies
# `F: RawDataSerializable` and every caller in the workspace compiles
# unchanged. Under the cfg the edge is gone. The generic code in p3-baby-bear's
# dependency graph that used the implication then states the bound itself
# (`F: … + RawDataSerializable`):
#   - the three extension-field impls of `RawDataSerializable`, and
#   - the six `SerializingHasher` impls in p3-symmetric.
# In a normal build these bounds are redundant, i.e. implied, so they change
# nothing. No expression, constant or body is changed.
#
# rustc checks it: extract.sh compiles p3-baby-bear under the cfg (what
# charon extracts) and the whole workspace without it (what upstream's tests
# run), both warning-free.
#
# Tested:     test-pre-patches.py: 6715 of 6769 upstream tests pass as
#             shipped, 6715 with the pre-patches; 0 divergences from this patch.
#
diff --git a/field/src/extension/binomial_extension.rs b/field/src/extension/binomial_extension.rs
